{"text": "Constance Hsu-Navarro\n2750 NW Arbor Crest Lane\nCorvallis, Oregon 97330\n(541) 555-0158  |  connie.hsunavarro@familymail.example\n\nNovember 2, 2026\n\nEvergreen Senior Health Plan\nAppeals Department\nP.O. Box 44170\nSalem, OR 97308-4170\nSent by fax to 1-866-555-0121 and by certified mail\n\nRE:  Request for reconsideration (Level 1 appeal)\n     Member: Florence Abernethy-Hsu\n     Member ID: ESH 0044 71920 01        Medicare no.: 4TK9-RW2-YH58\n     Date of birth: February 8, 1934\n     Claim no.: 2026-SNF-0098214\n     Dates of service denied: 09/21/2026 through 10/09/2026\n\nTo whom it may concern:\n\nI am Mrs. Abernethy-Hsu's daughter and I hold her health care power of attorney (copy\nenclosed). I am writing to appeal your Notice of Denial of Medical Coverage dated\nOctober 12, 2026, which refuses payment for nineteen days of skilled nursing care at\nWillamette Bend Rehabilitation & Care Center on the ground that the care was \"custodial.\"\n\nIt was not custodial. My mother is 92 years old. On September 14 she fell in her kitchen\nand broke her left hip. She had a partial hip replacement at Santiam Valley Medical Center\non September 15 and was discharged to Willamette Bend six days later on her surgeon's order.\nHer surgeon, Dr. Babajide Olatunji (NPI 1881746203), wrote the order for daily physical and\noccupational therapy and for skilled nursing to manage her warfarin and a\nstage 2 pressure wound on her heel. The therapy notes show she went from needing two people to stand to\nwalking sixty feet with a walker. That is the definition of skilled rehabilitation.\n\nYour denial says she \"plateaued\" on September 21. That is the day she arrived. I would\nlike to know who reviewed the file. Your letter also says she has advanced dementia. She\ndoes not. She has mild memory loss and does the crossword in pen.\n\nThe facility has billed us $11,343.00 ($597 a day for nineteen days). My mother lives on\nSocial Security and my late father's pension, about $2,900 a month. My brother Reginald Hsu\nand I have paid $4,000 of it so the facility would not send her to collections; I paid\nwith my own card (Visa ending 3637) and I expect that to be refunded when this is overturned.\n\nI am requesting an expedited reconsideration under 42 C.F.R. § 422.582 and a copy of\nthe complete case file, including the name and credentials of the reviewer.\n\nEnclosed: power of attorney; Dr. Olatunji's letter of October 20, 2026; therapy notes;\nfacility statement no. WB-77120-A; your denial; the Explanation of Benefits.\n\nIf you need her Social Security number to locate the file, the last four are 9427. Please\ncall me, not her. She is hard of hearing and the calls frighten her.\n\nSincerely,\n\nConstance Hsu-Navarro (Connie)\nDaughter and health care representative for Mrs. Abernethy-Hsu\n\ncc: Reggie Hsu; Oregon Senior Health Insurance Benefits Assistance", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "458 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Constance Hsu-Navarro", "Florence Abernethy-Hsu", "Dr. Babajide Olatunji", "Reginald Hsu"], "companies": ["Evergreen Senior Health Plan", "Willamette Bend Rehabilitation & Care Center", "Santiam Valley Medical Center", "Visa", "Oregon Senior Health Insurance Benefits Assistance"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Corvallis", "Oregon", "Salem", "OR"], "health": ["hip replacement", "skilled nursing", "warfarin", "stage 2 pressure wound", "advanced dementia", "mild memory loss", "hard of hearing", "therapy notes"], "sensitive": ["race or ethnicity", "Social Security number"], "names": ["Florence", "Constance", "connie", "Connie", "Reginald", "Olatunji"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.09999999403953552, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "street", "dob", "age90", "date", "p